# Mobile Modal Mini Tables

Mini tables (Account Details, Balances, Recent Activity) inside mobile account detail modals use tighter spacing than desktop to maximize content area on small screens.

## Row Padding

| Row type | Padding | Token |
|----------|---------|-------|
| **Section headers** (e.g. "Account Details", "Balances") | `spacing-xs` all sides | `["$O:spacing-xs", "$O:spacing-xs"]` |
| **Detail rows** | vertical `spacing-sm`, horizontal `spacing-xs` | `["$O:spacing-sm", "$O:spacing-xs"]` |
| **Footer rows** (e.g. "View All Accounts") | `spacing-xs` all sides | `["$O:spacing-xs", "$O:spacing-xs"]` |

## Other Mobile Modal Rules

- **Label column width**: 110px (narrower than description column to give values more room)
- **Modal padding**: `spacing-sm` (16px) on all sides
- **Header padding**: 0 (no extra padding on the header frame)
- **Header title font**: `typo-primary-lg-semibold` (not xl)
- **Institution logo**: 24×24px in the modal header
- **Body horizontal padding**: 0 (rows handle their own horizontal padding)
- **Account number eye icon**: text uses `width: "fit_content"` so the icon sits adjacent, not pushed to far right

## Scope

These conventions apply **only to mobile screens** with centered modal overlays. Desktop detail views use standard `spacing-sm` row padding.
